   "widgets_values": [
    "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> The Master: Japanese man about seventy, shaved head, short white beard trimmed close to the jaw, calm narrow eyes, dark charcoal silk kimono with a black haori and a small white family crest on the chest.\n<Prop> The Coin: a small round blue-grey steel coin with a circular single-wave crest.\n\nsummary:\nIn a quiet Edo-period room, the Master holds a small steel coin up to the window light, turns it once between two fingers and gives one slow nod. Calm, slow, no fast action.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] Medium close-up, eye level, very slow push-in. Golden tatami, shoji screens glowing with amber late-afternoon light, a dark alcove with an ink mountain scroll behind him. The Master raises the small steel coin with the wave crest between his thumb and index finger, turns it once so the light slides across the steel, studies it in silence, then gives one slow, satisfied nod.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet room tone, distant birdsong, the faint creak of the wooden floor, a soft metallic tick as the coin turns.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNone.",
