   "widgets_values": [
    "TWELVE JAPANESE BYTES · MiniMax H3 on a 12 GB card · Beyond the Frame\n\nRe-select your own model, encoder and VAE files in the loaders. Red = a teaching from the video.\n\n壱 SQUEEZE THE STEEL — 8-bit model (pruned INT8) + 4-bit text encoder (NVFP4).\n   https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3\n\n参 THE ATTENDANT (offloading) — ComfyUI moves weights to system RAM on its own.\n   Small card: start ComfyUI with  --lowvram  and have plenty of system RAM.\n   OOM with memory to spare?  --disable-dynamic-vram\n\n伍 CLEAR THE FLOOR — VRAM-Cleanup unloads every model, then the plain VAE Decode gets the whole card.\n   Install: ComfyUI Manager → 'Comfyui-Memory_Cleanup' (LAOGOU-666).\n   Update ComfyUI: the H3 decode got ~2× faster.\n\nFrames must fit n % 17 == 5: 124 (~5 s), 209 (~8.7 s), 243 (~10 s).\n\nDUEL TEST — run this graph first (baseline), then TJB_4_Pika_H3_Flex_6step.json and the HyperFlow\ntemplate with the same prompt, size, frames and seed. Note the 'Prompt executed in … s' time from the console."
   ]
  }
